  "scriptText": "Why does 朋友 (péngyǒu), the Chinese word for friend, feature two moons and two hands reaching out? Let's break down 朋 (péng) first. In ancient oracle bone script, 朋 (péng) depicted two strings of valuable cowrie shells tied side-by-side, which later evolved into two side-by-side moons 月 (yuè). It symbolizes two equal companions bound together by shared values! Now let's look at 友 (yǒu). Look closely at 友 (yǒu): it was originally drawn as two right hands, 𠂇 (yòu) and 又 (yòu), extending in the same direction! It represents two friends reaching out to support each other. Put them together, and 朋友 (péngyǒu) literally means companions standing side-by-side, extending helping hands in true friendship!",
